{
  "$doc": {
    "what": "Every file in this folder, in LOAD ORDER. tools/build.mjs injects them in this order (not alphabetical), tools/assemble-bank.mjs evaluates the headless ones in this order, and tools/test-module-contract.mjs holds every claim below against the running app. A *.js file that is not listed here fails the build. Read through tools/module-manifest.mjs, never directly.",
    "file": "File name inside src/app-modules.",
    "id": "Stable name other entries refer to. Renaming a file does not change it.",
    "kind": "content-pack (adds cards, doctrine, scenarios or terms to the bank as it loads) | feature (a screen or a service) | finalize (the one pass that tags and fingerprints the finished bank; every content-pack must load before it) | release-note (a What's New entry).",
    "headless": "true = tools/assemble-bank.mjs also evaluates this file with no page, so it must load cleanly with no DOM. Every content-pack and the finalize pass must be headless, or the content lints and the handheld card exporter never see what they add.",
    "requires": "ids of modules whose API this one calls. The build guarantees each of them loads EARLIER.",
    "uses": "ids of modules this one calls that load LATER. Only safe because those calls happen at run time, after every module has loaded - declared here so the exception is visible instead of implicit.",
    "provides": "Public API names other code may call (core, other modules, the shell scripts in src/, tools). Each must exist in the running app. A guarded call such as typeof G.x.y === \"function\" that points into a module must name something that module lists here.",
    "routes": "Routes whose screen this module draws. Each must be registered, and its render must call into this module.",
    "storageKeys": "Keys this module owns and writes in the app's on-device store (kv rows or localStorage). A trailing * is a prefix. Found by a static scan of the module's own write calls - it cannot see a write made on the module's behalf by a core API such as G.reminders.add or G.store.recordAttempt; those rows belong to core.",
    "clearsKeys": "Keys owned elsewhere that this module only deletes.",
    "optionalApis": "{ name, why }: a guarded API that may legitimately be missing, with the written reason. A guarded name that is missing and NOT listed (here or under core) fails the contract test; a listed name that exists in every build must be removed from the list.",
    "patches": "{ name, when, why }: a function owned by core or another module that this module REPLACES. when=load: swapped while the file loads (the contract test sees it happen and fails on an undeclared one). when=call: swapped for the length of one of the module's own calls and put back.",
    "hooks": "Named extension points (G.ext.on) this module subscribes to. The supported way to add to a core screen - no wrapping.",
    "core": "core.extensionPoints: the points src/index.html runs (G.ext.run). core.optionalApis: guarded APIs that live outside src/app-modules and may be missing."
  },
